// Regression test: `fail()` with zero arguments must be a clean compile
// error, not a compiler crash. `fail` is registered with a correct fixed
// arity (1) in Builtins.cpp, so TypeChecker::visitFuncCall's generic arity
// check DID already reject this -- but only in the mandatory main-pass
// TypeChecker run. main.cpp's earlier pre-pass runs its own TypeChecker
// instance first and deliberately discards its errors, then unconditionally
// codegens the same AST anyway (sub-pass 3b) -- reaching
// CodegenIntrinsic("fail", {}, ...)'s unchecked Args[0] and crashing the
// compiler (SIGABRT) before the mandatory pass ever got a chance to report
// the error cleanly. See src/Builtins.cpp's defensive Args.size() check on
// the "fail" branch (added as defense in depth for exactly this class of
// gap) and src/TypeChecker.cpp's visitFuncCall doc comment for the full
// story.

fn main(): int {
    fail();
    return 0;
}
